# 089-quickfix-interop-conversation: the conversation + probe scripts are
# DIGEST-BOUND. `_check_script_digest_binding` (tests/interop/
# cell_results_schema_check_test.py) SHA-256s the live file's raw bytes and
# compares against the digest recorded in the committed 400-witness evidence;
# conv_cell_test.cpp / probe_cell_test.cpp hash the same bytes at run time and
# compare against INTEROP_FIXPP_SCRIPT_DIGEST. A Windows checkout
# (core.autocrlf=true on the windows-msvc runners) CRLF-converts them, so the
# live hash becomes a06a8fc7… where the evidence records 8eada580… and the gate
# reds with a message that reads like a stale artifact rather than a line-ending
# conversion. MEASURED on run 34701080734, and reproduced exactly by
# `sed 's/$/\r/' conversation_script.yaml | sha256sum`.
#
# ⚠️ This is the FIFTH instance of this same trap (golden.hpp · Orchestra XML ·
# the enum-golden dictionaries + generator · the required-golden CSVs). Pin to
# LF, same class as every stanza above. The pattern to recognise: ANY file whose
# raw bytes are pinned by a value committed elsewhere needs a line here, and the
# symptom always names the artifact rather than the line endings.
# Regression guard: test_t095a_digest_bound_scripts_are_crlf_immune.
tests/interop/conversation/conversation_script.yaml -text
tests/interop/conversation/probe_script.yaml -text
